From 157c5b1b4939eae2257b04c035f1fd2fbd7b65ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabriel Zim <info@zimcontent.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:13:51 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] fix(runner): with a person in control, only their
 commands reach the daemon

While the stream is in "control", a browser.act, batch or capture that is
not the person's no longer enters agent-browser's queue: `get url` and
`get title` are answered from what the stream showed, and the rest comes
back at once with `person_in_control`. The address bar and the restart
send `person: true` and still run. The handoffs' keep-alive does not read
the address of a browser someone drives from here, and taking control
again no longer makes the person's input wait 30 s: only an agent's
command cut midway does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
